I walk over to a small kiosk in the sports hall.
A young man stands behind the counter.
He smiles and says hello.
"Hello, I want to play badminton today," I say.
"Are you new here in the club?" he asks.
"Yes, I would like to try to join in," I answer.
"Welcome," the man says.
"Do you need to rent a racket?" he asks.
"Yes please, I want to rent a racket for the evening," I say.
He finds a good racket for me.
"It costs forty kroner," he says.
I take out my payment card.
I pay the forty kroner.
He gives me the racket over the counter.
"I think it is a fun sport," I say happily.
"It is also a really fun sport," he smiles.
"Have a really good game."
I say thank you and walk over to the courts.
